Problem Statement
Write a Java program that:
1.	Demonstrates the use of nested try blocks.
2.	Outer try block should contain two inner try blocks:
o	First inner try: Divide two integers (handle ArithmeticException).
o	Second inner try: Access an invalid array index (handle ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException).
3.	Each exception should be handled separately with an appropriate message.
4.	Print a final message at the end to indicate completion of program execution.
Requirements
•	Use nested try–catch blocks properly.
•	Use try–catch–finally structure to demonstrate normal flow.
•	Handle:
o	ArithmeticException — division by zero
o	ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException — accessing invalid array index
•	Use meaningful messages for each exception.
